The copy constructor is already a minimal member-wise copy with an inline-friendly initializer list, so there is nothing to remove; I kept it identical to avoid any behavioural change while letting the compiler inline the trivial member copies.

```cpp
Field::Field(const Field &field)
    : FieldBase(field)
    , profile(field.profile)
    , profileIndex(field.profileIndex)
    , type(field.type)
    , isFieldExpanded(field.isFieldExpanded)
{
}
```